From ee8529e9dc9a9b060a3b34fc7e877ae3d4ca2f09 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Stefan Ceriu <stefanc@matrix.org>
Date: Tue, 13 Oct 2026 13:20:50 +0300
Subject: [PATCH 07/11] perf(search): Don't stretch the search index passphrase

The passphrase is already a high-entropy key, yet opening each room's encrypted index ran PBKDF2 (10k rounds) to unwrap a per-room key, ~80% of a cold open. Derive the file keys straight from the passphrase with HKDF instead, and drop the key file. Indexes that can't be opened, including the ones in the old format, are recreated.

(cherry picked from commit b51ccdaa7824e5568902701eb85c2d9f6c44672a)
