+Encrypted room indexes no longer stretch the passphrase with PBKDF2, which made opening each index slow: the
+passphrase must now be a high-entropy key. Existing encrypted indexes, and any index that can't be opened (e.g. after
+a passphrase change), are deleted and recreated.
